From: The open-edison contributors
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] spi: pxa2xx-pci: use PIO on Merrifield SSP5

On the Intel Edison (Merrifield), a transfer on SSP5 long enough to use
DMA (8 bytes or more) times out, and a CPU then stalls, hanging the
board. SSP5 is the SPI on the Edison's Arduino expansion board header.

Don't set up DMA for SSP5, so every transfer uses PIO, of any length.
---
diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx-pci.c b/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx-pci.c
index cae77ac..1c8ba51 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx-pci.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx-pci.c
@@ -225,6 +225,14 @@ static int mrfld_spi_setup(struct pci_dev *dev, struct pxa2xx_spi_controller *c)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;

+	/*
+	 * DMA on SSP5 hangs the Intel Edison: a transfer long enough to use it
+	 * (8 bytes or more) times out, then a CPU stalls. Use PIO for every
+	 * transfer on that port.
+	 */
+	if (ssp->port_id == 5)
+		return 0;
+
 	dma_dev = pci_get_slot(dev->bus, PCI_DEVFN(21, 0));
 	ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(&dev->dev, lpss_dma_put_device, dma_dev);
 	if (ret)
